From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: Wait for the soft-stopped slots with the live
 slot status

panfrost_reset() soft-stops the slots and waits for them to go idle by
polling JOB_INT_JS_STATE. That register is not live: it is a snapshot of
the slot states taken when JOB_INT_CLEAR was last written (the Arm driver
documents it as "status==active and _next == busy snapshot from last
JOB_IRQ_CLEAR"). A job that was started into an idle slot, the usual case
for an OpenCL queue that submits one kernel at a time, still shows the slot
idle, and the wait ends at once while the job is still stopping.

With the GPU reset that followed, the stale wait did not matter: the reset
killed the job anyway. Since the previous patch resumes a still-active job
without the reset, it does. The sequence then is: the wait returns at
once, the pending interrupts are handled (there are none yet), the job is
removed from pfdev->jobs[], and it is resubmitted from its old head while
the hardware is still running its first incarnation under a soft-stop.
Two things can happen when the first incarnation then finishes:

 - it reports STOPPED: the error interrupt handler cancels _NEXT (the
   resubmission), dequeues the job and records the resume tail, and nothing
   starts it again. 500 ms later the watchdog finds the slot idle, status
   STOPPED instead of ACTIVE, and resets the GPU after all;

 - it reports DONE (the job was about to finish when it was stopped): the
   handler dequeues the resubmission's entry and signals the fence, the
   job manager starts the resubmission from _NEXT, and that second run
   completes on a slot we have no job for:

   Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000000000f8
   pc : panfrost_dequeue_job+0x2c/0xd8 [panfrost]
   lr : panfrost_jm_handle_irqs+0x268/0x570 [panfrost]
    panfrost_jm_irq_handler_thread+0x1c/0x60 [panfrost]

   (seen on a Mali-G31 running the OpenCL CTS Integer Ops long16 division
   kernels, about two minutes in), followed by a hang of
   panfrost_jm_ctx_destroy() and a lockup of the panfrost-reset workqueue.

Wait for the slots on the live JS_STATUS registers instead: a slot is busy
while it reads ACTIVE, and every slot has to be idle before the queues are
touched. The pending DONE or STOPPED interrupt is then handled before the
resubmission, which skips a finished job and resumes a stopped one from its
tail, as intended. Hold a runtime PM reference across the stop and the
resubmission, since the stopped jobs drop theirs in between and a suspend
would power the L2 off under the soft-stopped job. And make
panfrost_dequeue_job() return NULL for a slot without a job: every caller
copes with a NULL, so a stray event is a warning rather than an Oops.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 1 file changed, 33 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
@@ -163,7 +163,12 @@
 {
 	struct panfrost_job *job = pfdev->jobs[slot][0];
 
-	WARN_ON(!job);
+	/* An event for a slot we have no job on: a resubmission raced with
+	 * the first run of the job (see panfrost_reset()). Not fatal, as
+	 * every caller copes with a NULL job; a WARN, not an Oops.
+	 */
+	if (WARN_ON(!job))
+		return NULL;
 
 	if (job->is_profiled && job->engine_usage) {
 		job->engine_usage->elapsed_ns[slot] +=
@@ -632,39 +637,42 @@
 	}
 }
 
-static u32 panfrost_active_slots(struct panfrost_device *pfdev,
-				 u32 *js_state_mask, u32 js_state)
+/* A slot is busy as long as its status register reads ACTIVE. This has to
+ * be the live JS_STATUS: JOB_INT_JS_STATE is a snapshot taken when
+ * JOB_INT_CLEAR was last written, so for a job that was started into an idle
+ * slot it still shows the slot idle, and a wait on it ends before the
+ * soft-stop has done anything.
+ */
+static bool panfrost_slots_idle(struct panfrost_device *pfdev)
 {
-	u32 rawstat;
-
-	if (!(js_state & *js_state_mask))
-		return 0;
+	unsigned int i;
 
-	rawstat = job_read(pfdev, JOB_INT_RAWSTAT);
-	if (rawstat) {
-		unsigned int i;
-
-		for (i = 0; i < NUM_JOB_SLOTS; i++) {
-			if (rawstat & MK_JS_MASK(i))
-				*js_state_mask &= ~MK_JS_MASK(i);
-		}
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_JOB_SLOTS; i++) {
+		if (job_read(pfdev, JS_STATUS(i)) ==
+		    DRM_PANFROST_EXCEPTION_ACTIVE)
+			return false;
 	}
 
-	return js_state & *js_state_mask;
+	return true;
 }
 
 static void
 panfrost_reset(struct panfrost_device *pfdev,
 	       struct drm_sched_job *bad, bool job_active)
 {
-	u32 js_state, js_state_mask = 0xffffffff;
 	unsigned int i, j;
-	bool cookie;
+	bool cookie, idle;
 	int ret;
 
 	if (!atomic_read(&pfdev->reset.pending))
 		return;
 
+	/* The jobs we stop drop their runtime PM references before we submit
+	 * them again. Keep the GPU powered in between: a suspend would power
+	 * the L2 off and lose the dirty lines of a soft-stopped job.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_get_noresume(pfdev->base.dev);
+
 	/* Stop the schedulers.
 	 *
 	 * FIXME: We temporarily get out of the dma_fence_signalling section
@@ -702,10 +710,14 @@
 	/* Wait at most 10ms for soft-stops to complete. A job that was still
 	 * active gets 100ms: the soft-stop lets the tasks already issued run
 	 * to completion, and a long compute kernel has hundreds in flight.
+	 * Every slot must have gone idle before we touch the queues: a job
+	 * that is still stopping (or finishing) raises its interrupt later,
+	 * when its entry in pfdev->jobs[] is gone or belongs to its own
+	 * resubmission, and the second start of that job then runs on a slot
+	 * we have no job for.
 	 */
-	ret = readl_poll_timeout(pfdev->iomem + JOB_INT_JS_STATE, js_state,
-				 !panfrost_active_slots(pfdev, &js_state_mask, js_state),
-				 10, job_active ? 100000 : 10000);
+	ret = read_poll_timeout(panfrost_slots_idle, idle, idle, 10,
+				job_active ? 100000 : 10000, false, pfdev);
 
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(pfdev->base.dev, "Soft-stop failed\n");
@@ -769,6 +781,8 @@
 	panfrost_jm_enable_interrupts(pfdev);
 
 	dma_fence_end_signalling(cookie);
+
+	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(pfdev->base.dev);
 }
 
 static enum drm_gpu_sched_stat panfrost_job_timedout(struct drm_sched_job
